{"accessed_at":"2026-11-08T05:51:16.813Z","result":"Manual Difco (https://cdn.media.interlabdist.com.br/uploads/2021/01/LB-Lennox-Agar-e-Broth-.pdf)\nciteturn70search12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; **Difco™ LB Broth, Lennox** ... | Tryptone | 10.0 g |\nLB Agar, Lennox • LB Broth, Lennox\n\n## Intended Use\nLB Agar, Lennox and LB Broth, Lennox are used for maintaining and cultivating recombinant strains of *Escherichia coli*.\n\n## Summary and Explanation\nLB Agar, Lennox and LB Broth, Lennox are nutritionally rich media developed by Lennox for the growth and maintenance of pure cultures of recombinant strains of *E. coli*.<sup>1</sup> These strains are generally derived from *E. coli* K12, which are deficient in B vitamin production. This strain of *E. coli* has been further modified through specific mutation to create an auxotrophic strain that is not capable of growth on nutritionally deficient media.\n\nLB Agar, Lennox provides all the nutritional requirements of these organisms. LB Agar, Lennox contains half the sodium chloride level of the Miller formulation of LB Agar.<sup>2</sup> This allows the researcher to select the optimal salt concentration for a specific strain.\n\nLB Broth, Lennox contains ten times the sodium chloride level of Luria Broth Base, Miller and one half of that found in LB Broth, Miller.<sup>3</sup> This allows the researcher to select the optimal salt concentration for a specific strain. If desired, the medium may be aseptically supplemented with glucose to prepare the complete medium described by Lennox.\n\n## User Quality Control\n\n### Identity Specifications\n\n**Difco™ LB Agar, Lennox**\n\n| Specification | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Dehydrated Appearance | Light beige, free-flowing, homogeneous. |\n| Solution | 3.5% solution, soluble in purified water upon boiling. Solution is medium amber, clear to slightly opalescent. |\n| Prepared Appearance | Medium amber, very slightly to slightly opalescent. |\n| Reaction of 3.5% Solution at 25°C | pH 7.0 ± 0.2 |\n\n**Difco™ LB Broth, Lennox**\n\n| Specification | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Dehydrated Appearance | Light beige, free-flowing, homogeneous. |\n| Solution | 2.0% solution, soluble in purified water. Solution is light amber, clear to very slightly opalescent. |\n| Prepared Appearance | Very light amber, clear to very slightly opalescent. |\n| Reaction of 2.0% Solution at 25°C | pH 7.0 ± 0.2 |\n\n### Cultural Response\nDifco™ LB Agar, Lennox or LB Broth, Lennox. Prepare the medium per label directions. Inoculate and incubate at 35 ± 2°C for 18–24 hours.\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n\n| Organism | ATCC™ | Inoculum CFU | Recovery Agar | Recovery Broth |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| *Escherichia coli* | 23724 (C600) | 10²–3×10² | Good | N/A |\n| *Escherichia coli* | 33694 (HB101) | 10²–3×10² | Good | Good |\n| *Escherichia coli* | 33849 (DH1) | 10²–3×10² | Good | N/A |\n| *Escherichia coli* | 39403 (JM103) | 10²–3×10² | Good | Good |\n| *Escherichia coli* | 47014 (JM107) | 10²–3×10² | Good | N/A |\n| *Escherichia coli* | 53868 (DH5) | 10²–3×10² | Good | Good |\n\n</table>\n\n## Principles of the Procedure\nPeptone provides nitrogen and carbon. Vitamins (including B vitamins) and certain trace elements are provided by yeast extract. Sodium ions for transport and osmotic balance are provided by sodium chloride. Agar is the solidifying agent in LB Agar, Lennox.\n\n## Formulae\n\n**Difco™ LB Agar, Lennox**\n\n<table id=\"e2\">\n\n| Approximate Formula* Per Liter | Amount |\n|---|---:|\n| Tryptone | 10.0 g |\n| Yeast Extract | 5.0 g |\n| Sodium Chloride | 5.0 g |\n| Agar | 15.0 g |\n\n</table>\n\n**Difco™ LB Broth, Lennox**  \nConsists of the same ingredients without the agar.  \n*Adjusted and/or supplemented as required to meet performance criteria.*\n\n## Directions for Preparation from Dehydrated Product\n1. Suspend/dissolve the powder in 1 L of purified water:  \n   Difco™ LB Agar, Lennox – 35 g;  \n   Difco™ LB Broth, Lennox – 20 g.  \n   Mix thoroughly.\n2. Heat the agar medium with frequent agitation and boil for 1 minute to completely dissolve the powder.\n3. Autoclave at 121°C for 15 minutes.\n4. Test samples of the finished product for performance using stable, typical control cultures.\n\n## Procedure\nConsult appropriate references for recommended test procedures.<sup>1–4</sup>\n\n## Expected Results\nAfter sufficient incubation, the agar medium should show growth as evidenced by formation of colonies and/or a confluent lawn of growth. In the broth medium, growth is evident by the appearance of turbidity.\n\n## References\n1. Lennox. 1955. *Virology* 1:190.\n2. Ausubel, Brent, Kingston, Moore, Seidman, Smith and Struhl (ed.). 1994. *Current protocols in molecular biology*, vol. 1. Green Publishing Associates, Inc., Brooklyn, N.Y.\n3. Miller. 1972. *Experiments in molecular genetics*. Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory, Cold Spring Harbor, N.Y.\n4. Sambrook, Fritsch and Maniatis. 1989. *Molecular cloning: a laboratory manual*, 2nd ed. Cold Spring Harbor Laboratory Press, Cold Spring Harbor, N.Y.\n\n## Availability\n\n**Difco™ LB Agar, Lennox**  \nCat. No. 240110 — Dehydrated – 500 g\n\n**Difco™ LB Broth, Lennox**\n\n| Cat. No. | Product |\n|---|---|\n| 240230 | Dehydrated – 500 g |\n| 240210 | Dehydrated – 2 kg |\n| 240220 | Dehydrated – 10 kg |--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nManual Difco (https://cdn.media.interlabdist.com.br/uploads/2021/01/LB-Miller-Agar-e-Broth-.pdf)\nciteturn70search13 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; LB Broth, Miller contains twenty times the sodium chloride level of Luria Broth Base, Miller and twice the level found in LB Broth, Lennox. ... **Difco™ LB Broth, Miller** ... 10.0 g\n\n### Identity Specifications\n\n**Difco™ LB Agar, Miller**  \nDehydrated Appearance: Light tan, free-flowing, homogeneous.  \nSolution: 4.0% solution, soluble in purified water upon boiling. Solution is light amber, very slightly to slightly opalescent.  \nPrepared Appearance: Very light amber, slightly opalescent.  \nReaction of 4.0% Solution at 25°C: pH 7.0 ± 0.2\n\n**Difco™ LB Broth, Miller**  \nDehydrated Appearance: Off-white to beige, free-flowing, homogeneous.  \nSolution: 2.5% solution; soluble in purified water. Solution is light amber, clear to very slightly opalescent.  \nPrepared Appearance: Very light amber, clear to very slightly opalescent.  \nReaction of 2.5% Medium at 25°C: pH 7.0 ± 0.2\n\n### Cultural Response\n**Difco™ LB Agar, Miller or LB Broth, Miller**  \nPrepare the medium per label directions. Inoculate and incubate at 35 ± 2°C for 18-24 hours.\n\n<table id=\"e1\">\n<tr><th>ORGANISM</th><th>ATCC™</th><th>INOCULUM CFU</th><th>RECOVERY</th></tr>\n<tr><td><i>Escherichia coli</i></td><td>33526 (K802)</td><td>10²-10³</td><td>Good</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n## Principles of the Procedure\nPeptone provides nitrogen and carbon. Vitamins (including B vitamins) and certain trace elements are provided by yeast extract. Sodium ions for transport and osmotic balance are provided by sodium chloride. Agar is the solidifying agent in LB Agar, Miller.\n\n## Formulae\n\n**Difco™ LB Agar, Miller**  \nApproximate Formula* Per Liter  \nTryptone .................................................. 10.0 g  \nYeast Extract ............................................. 5.0 g  \nSodium Chloride ........................................ 10.0 g  \nAgar .......................................................... 15.0 g\n\n**Difco™ LB Broth, Miller**  \nConsists of the same ingredients without the agar.  \n*Adjusted and/or supplemented as required to meet performance criteria.\n\n## Directions for Preparation from Dehydrated Product\n1. Suspend/dissolve the powder in 1 L of purified water:  \n   Difco™ LB Agar, Miller – 40 g;  \n   Difco™ LB Broth, Miller – 25 g.  \n   Mix thoroughly.\n2. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(19)\nTEPZZ 4¥¥64 B_T\n(11)\nEP 2 433 642 B1\n(12)\nEUR (https://patentimages.storage.googleapis.com/c7/4d/00/c8e550bb9b9531/EP2433642B1.pdf)\nciteturn70search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; 500 μl of LB (LB; Difco LB Broth Lennox, approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0\nThe cells were incubated the plasmid DNA on ice for 30\nminutes, and then heat shocked at 42°C for 45 seconds. The cells were then incubated on ice for 2 minutes for recovery.\n500 μl of LB (LB; Difco LB Broth Lennox, approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0\ng Sodium Chloride) was added to the cells, and the culture was incubated at 37°C with shaking for 1 hour. 50 μl of the\ncells was then plated out on agar plates containing 50 μg/ml carbenicillin for selection. The plate was incubated at 37°C\nfor 16-18 hours.\n[0507]\n25 ml of LB containing 50 μg/ml carbenicillin was inoculated from a single colony and grown until fully confluent.\n0.5 ml of the seed culture was added to 800 ml of 2XYT containing 10 μg/ml of carbenicillin and grown overnight (∼12-16\nhours; approximately 44 flasks). The cells were harvested by centrifugation at 6,000 x g in a Sorvall rotor # SLC4000.\nThe cell pellets were pooled and weighed. From 35.2 L of E. coli culture, 320 g of wet cell pellet was obtained. 600 ml\nof a buffer containing 50 mM Potassium Phosphate (KPO4) pH 7.4 and 300 mM Sodium Chloride (NaCl) was added to\nthe cell pellet. After the cells were completely resuspended, the batch was split into two and each part was sonicated\n116--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(19)\nTEPZZ_94Z457B_T\n(11)\nEP 1 940 457 B1\n(12)\nEUR (https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/publication-dates/20121212/patents/EP1940457NWB1/document.pdf)\nciteturn70search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.4 years ago; 500 ml of LB (LB; Difco LB Broth Lennox, approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0\n45 and 60 minutes indicating cardiac damage at these time points.\nExample 26\nExpression and Purification of Modified MT-SP1 CB238 in shake flasks\n50\n55\n[0484]\nCB238 and related recombinant MT-SP1 mutants or wild-type MT-SP1 were cloned and expressed in E.coli\nas inclusion bodies as described in Example 1 and 2 above. The production of the MT-SP1 or mutants was adapted for\nlaboratory scale by optimizing production of the MT-SP1 mutant CB238 by pooling up to about 44 X 1L shake flasks for\nsubsequent isolation of the inclusion body pellets for solubilization and refolding. Briefly, 1 ml of plasmid DNA (from DNA\nminiprep purification) was mixed with 50 ml of BL-21 cells. The cells were incubated the plasmid DNA on ice for 30\nminutes, and then heat shocked at 42°C for 45 seconds. The cells were then incubated on ice for 2 minutes for recovery.\n500 ml of LB (LB; Difco LB Broth Lennox, approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0\ng Sodium Chloride) was added to the cells, and the culture was incubated at 37°C with shaking for 1 hour. 50 ml of the\n113--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnderstanding the Compositional Changes in LB Lennox Medium during Growth of Escherichia Coli DH5α in a 1L Bioreactor (https://cdn.fortunejournals.com/articles/understanding-the-compositional-changes-in-lb-lennox-medium-during-growth-of-escherichia-coli-dh5alpha-in-a-1l-bioreactor.pdf)\nciteturn70search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.9 years ago; Crawled: today; Seeking to understand the compositional changes to LB Lennox medium as *Escherichia coli* DH5α (ATCC 53868) grows in it, gel filtration chromatography (GFC) and C-18 reversed phase high performance liquid chromatography (RP-HPLC) were used to characterize the changes to the culture broth with growth of the bacterium. ... LB Lennox medium was purchased from Difco and has the following composition [g/L]: Tryptone, 10.0; Yeast Extract, 5.0; NaCl, 5.0.\nSamples collected at regular time points in the culture were analysed by both gel filtration chromatography for understanding the molecular weight changes in the different fractions present, as well as RP-HPLC for determining the different fractions.\n\nResults revealed that the gel filtration column used was unable to detect molecular weight changes of a few Da to few hundred Da. Three broad peaks were seen in the eluted chromatogram from gel filtration chromatography, indicating that the column was unable to distinguish fractions beyond the three broad ones detected. Reversed phase high performance liquid chromatography, on the other hand, was also unable to fractionate LB Lennox broth given the complexity of the microbiological medium. Additionally, 194 nm was validated to be a useful wavelength for visualizing the RP-HPLC chromatogram of LB Lennox medium given the significant increase in information available at this wavelength compared to 280, 264 and 254 nm.\n\n## 2. Material and Methodology\n\n### 2.1 Materials\n\nLB Lennox medium was purchased from Difco and has the following composition [g/L]: Tryptone, 10.0; Yeast Extract, 5.0; NaCl, 5.0. Polyethylene glycol antifoam was purchased from Sigma-Aldrich.\n\n---\n\nInternational Journal of Applied Biology and Pharmaceutical Technology  \nVol. 12 No. 4 - December 2021.  \n483--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUnderstanding the Compositional Changes in LB Lennox Medium during Growth of Escherichia Coli DH5α in a 1L Bioreactor (https://www.academia.edu/65286188/Understanding_the_Compositional_Changes_in_LB_Lennox_Medium_during_Growth_of_Escherichia_Coli_DH5%CE%B1_in_a_1L_Bioreactor)\nciteturn70search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.9 years ago; Crawled: today; Material and Methodology 2.1 Materials LB Lennox medium was purchased from Difco and has the following composition [g/L]: Tryptone, 10.0; Yeast Extract, 5.0; NaCl, 5.0. ... Detection by diode array detector at 194 nm, Column: Agilent Technologies Poroshell 120 SBC18, Flow rate = 0.2 ml/min, 5/95 Ethanol/water (%/%) for isocratic elution, 25 oC, 70 bar pressure, Injection volume = 10 µL Elution of LB Lennox broth at 1 hour post inoculation from C-18 RP-HPLC is shown in Figure 9, which indicated the complexity of the broth that precludes clean separation by RPHPLC, as well as the presence of large amounts of hydrophilic compounds which could be desorbed by a 5% ethanol/95% water mixture.\n 2. Material and Methodology 2.1 Materials LB Lennox medium was purchased from Difco and has the following composition [g/L]: Tryptone, 10.0; Yeast Extract, 5.0; NaCl, 5.0. Polyethylene glycol antifoam was purchased from Sigma-Aldrich. International Journal of Applied Biology and Pharmaceutical Technology Vol. 12 No. 4 - December 2021. 483 Int J Appl Biol Pharm 2021; 12 (4): 481-491 DOI: 10.26502/ijabpt.202114 2.2 Growth of Escherichia coli DH5α in Bioreactor Glycerol stock culture of Escherichia coli DH5α (ATCC 53868), kept at -70 oC prior to inoculation, was used in inoculating a 100 mL LB Lennox medium in a 250 mL glass shake flask. Cultivation of the aerobic seed culture was at 37 oC and 230 rpm rotational shaking in a temperature controlled incubator. After 14 hours of incubation, 5 mL of the seed culture was used in inoculating 500 mL of LB Lennox medium and 50 mL of 100 g/L polyethylene glycol antifoam. Stirring speed was 400 rpm with 1 VVM aeration. Temperature was controlled at 37 oC, with no control for pH. At appropriate time points, 5 mL of broth was collected for analysis of pH and optical density. Optical density was measured with a Shimadzu Biospec-Mini spectrophotometer using a quartz cuvette of 1 cm path length, where appropriate dilution with deionized water was used if optical density exceeded 1. pH was measured with an Orion pH probe fitted on a Sartorius pH meter. 2.3 Gel Filtration Chromatography (GFC) Waters gel filtration chromatography instrument was calibrated with polyethylene glycol molecular weight standards prior to the experiment. Refractive index detector was used for detection, and the column and detector temperatures were at 35oC. 0.1g of the molecular weight standards were dissolved in 100 mL of ultrapure water one day prior to the analysis and the constituted standards filtered through 0.45 µm nylon membrane filter. Molecular weight markers used were 1460 Da, 7130 Da, 12900 Da, and 20600 Da.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nModified proteases that inhibit complement activation (https://patents.google.com/patent/WO2007047995A2/no)\nciteturn70search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 19.6 years ago; Crawled: last month; l of LB (LB; Difco LB Broth Lennox, approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0 g Sodium Chloride) was added to the cells, and the culture was incubated at 37 0 C with shaking for 1 hour.\n  * the rate of increase in LV pressure levels in rabbits perfused in the presence of CB200 remained low at 45 and 60 minutes indicating cardiac damage at these time points.\n  * Example 26 Expression and Purification of Modified MT-SPl CB238 in shake flasks CB238 and related recombinant MT-SPl mutants or wild-type MT-SPl were cloned and expressed in E.coli as inclusion bodies as described in Example 1 and 2 above.\n  * the production of the MT-SPl or mutants was adapted for laboratory scale by optimizing production of the MT-SPl mutant CB238 by pooling up to about 44 X 1 L shake flasks for subsequent isolation of the inclusion body pellets for solubilization and refolding. Briefly, 1 ⁇ l of plasmid DNA (from DNA miniprep purification) was mixed with 50 ⁇ l of BL-21 cells.\n  * the cells were incubated the plasmid DNA on ice for 30 minutes, and then heat shocked at 42 0 C for 45 seconds. The cells were then incubated on ice for 2 minutes for recovery. 500 ⁇ l of LB (LB; Difco LB Broth Lennox, approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0 g Sodium Chloride) was added to the cells, and the culture was incubated at 37 0 C with shaking for 1 hour. 50 ⁇ l of the cells was then plated out on agar plates containing 50 ⁇ g/ml carbenicillin for selection. The plate was incubated at 37 0 C for 16-18 hours.\n  * LB LB\n  * Difco LB Broth Lennox approximate formulation per liter: 10.0 g Tryptone, 10.0 g Yeast Extract, 5.0 g Sodium Chloride\n  * the supernatant was poured out and replaced with -300 ml of fresh buffer containing 50 mM KPO 4 pH 7.4, 300 mM NaCl, and 0.5% lauryldimethylamine oxide (LDAO) volume/volume.\n  * the inclusion body was resuspended using a spatula and the solution was stirred until homogenous. The stirred sample was then centrifuged again and the supernatant decanted.\n  * the LDAO wash was performed a total of three times followed by three rounds of washing with buffer containing 50 mM KPO 4 pH 7.4, 300 mM NaCl that does not contain LDAO.\n  * the resulting protein solution was concentrated by hollow filtration to ⁇ 1-2L then dialyzed into 16 L of buffer containing 50 mM Tris pH 8.0, 50 mM NaCl at 4°C overnight.\n  * the buffer was exchanged for fresh buffer the following morning, and the sample was dialyzed for an additional 8 hours.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBD Difco LB Broth (Lennox) LB培養液 (分生實驗重組大腸桿菌增殖) - 全研生技 - 微生物培養基｜細胞培養耗材｜實驗室耗材 (https://tr-bio.ipedia.tw/product/lb-broth-lennox/)\nciteturn70search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; # BD Difco LB Broth (Lennox) LB培養液 (分生實驗重組大腸桿菌增殖) ... Tryptone ………………………………………………………….10.0 g\n若需要，也可在無菌條件下添加葡萄糖，以製備成 Lennox 完整培養配方。\n\n## 〖培養基原理〗\n\n其組成原理如下：蛋白腖（Peptone）提供氮源與碳源；酵母萃取物（Yeast Extract）提供維生素（尤其是B群）與微量元素；氯化鈉（NaCl）則供應鈉離子以維持滲透壓平衡；固體培養基中添加的瓊脂（Agar）則作為凝固劑使用。\n\n本產品特別適合用於基因工程研究、質體擴增、生物轉殖等應用中對 E. coli 重組菌株的培養與保存。\n\n## 〖原廠成分表參考〗\n\n  * ## pH 7.0 ± 0.2\n\n  * ## Difco ™ LB Broth, Lennox\n\nApproximate Formula* Per Liter\nTryptone ………………………………………………………….10.0 g\nYeast Extract ………………………………………………………5.0 g\nSodium Chloride ………………………………………………… 5.0 g\n\n## 〖特性規格〗\n\n  * 脫水狀態為淺米色（light beige），質地均勻且易流動（free-flowing, homogeneous）。\n  * 按建議濃度（2.0%）溶解於純化水中，可完全溶解，所得溶液為淺琥珀色（light amber），呈現清澈至極輕微乳白狀（clear to very slightly opalescent）。\n  * 配置完成的培養基外觀亦為非常淺琥珀色，清澈至略微乳白，屬正常現象，不影響使用。\n\n## 〖使用方法〗\n\n  1. 懸浮／溶解培養基粉末於 1 公升純化水中：LB Broth, Lennox：20 克 , 充分混合均勻。\n\n  2. 對於 LB Agar（固體培養基），需持續攪拌並加熱至沸騰 1 分鐘，確保粉末完全溶解。\n\n  3. 將培養基於 121°C 高壓滅菌 15 分鐘。\n\n  4. 使用穩定且具代表性的品質控制菌株測試成品，以驗證培養基之性能表現與品質一致性。--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLB media Lennox (https://shop.gmexpression.com/LB-Lennox)\nciteturn70search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; The GMExpression formulation is supplied as pre-weighed dehydrated base in both Lennox (5 g/L NaCl, ATCC Medium 271, BD Difco 240230) and Miller (10 g/L NaCl, BD Difco 244620) variants. ... Use LB Lennox + 10 mM MgSO_{4} + 0.2 % w/v maltose.\n\n## Composition — per 1 L equivalent unless stated otherwise\n\n### LB Lennox (Bertani 1951 / ATCC Medium 271 / BD Difco 240230; per 1 L)\n\nComponent  | Concentration  | Function\n--- | --- | ---\nTryptone (pancreatic digest of casein)  | 10.0 g  | Free amino acid and small-peptide nitrogen source; E. coli primary growth substrate\nYeast extract  | 5.0 g  | B-vitamins (biotin, thiamine, niacin, riboflavin, pantothenate), purines / pyrimidines, trace minerals; accelerates lag-phase exit\nSodium chloride (NaCl)  | 5.0 g  | Osmotic balance (86 mM); preserves outer-membrane LPS lattice; preferred for sensitive phages\n\nTotal dry solids: 20 g/L. Pre-autoclaving pH: 7.0 ± 0.2 at 25 °C (rarely needs adjustment with the commercial-grade powder).\n\n### LB Miller (BD Difco 244620; per 1 L)\n\nComponent  | Concentration  | Function\n--- | --- | ---\nTryptone  | 10.0 g  | As above\nYeast extract  | 5.0 g  | As above\nSodium chloride (NaCl)  | 10.0 g  | Higher osmolarity (170 mM); preferred for fermenter-scale growth and industrial recombinant protein expression\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBD DIFCO LB Broth (Miller) LB培養液 LB肉湯 - 全研生技 - 微生物培養基｜細胞培養耗材｜實驗室耗材 (https://tr-bio.ipedia.tw/product/lb-broth-miller/)\nciteturn70search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; # BD DIFCO LB Broth (Miller) LB培養液 LB肉湯 ... LB Broth, Miller 的氯化鈉濃度為 Luria Broth Base, Miller 的 20 倍，亦為 LB Broth, Lennox 的 2 倍，研究者可依不同菌株的需求選擇最適鹽濃度進行培養。 ... Tryptone ………………………………………………………….10.0  g\n\n## 〖原廠成分表參考〗\n\n  * ### 產品pH值：7.0 ± 0.2\n\n  * ### Difco ™  LB Broth, miller\n\nApproximate Formula* Per Liter\n\nTryptone ………………………………………………………….10.0  g\n\nYeast Extract ………………………………………………………5.0  g\n\nSodium Chloride ………………………………………………. 10.0  g\n\n## 〖特性規格〗\n\n脫水培養基外觀：淺褐色，自由流動，均質一致。\n\n溶液：4.0% 溶液，可在加熱至沸騰時溶解於純化水中。溶液呈淺琥珀色，極輕微至輕微乳白狀。\n\n配製後外觀：非常淺的琥珀色，略為乳白狀。\n\n## 〖使用方法〗\n\n1.         將粉末懸浮／溶解於 1 公升純化水中：Difco™ LB Broth, Miller – 25 克。充分混合。\n\n2.         持續攪拌並加熱至沸騰 1 分鐘，使粉末完全溶解。\n\n3.         以 121°C 高壓滅菌 15 分鐘。\n\n4.         使用穩定且典型的對照菌株測試成品的性能。--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChloride Powder HSN 3821 Exports from US Mar-26 | Volza (https://www.volza.com/p/chloride-powder/hsn-code-3821/export-data/exports-from-united-states/)\nciteturn70search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago; HSN Code 3821000000  | Product Description DO_ 06277535 OEA CODE_ 0334 DI_ 6 OF 25 PRODUCT: BD DIFCO LB BROTH, MILLER (LURIA-BERTANI) - CULTIVATION MEDIUM. COMPOSITION: TRYPTONE 10.0 G, YEAST EXTRACT 5.0 G, SODIUM CHLORIDE 10.0 G. ... (1 UNIT); Product: LB broth (Lennox) Medium of microbial growth powder, composition: 50% triptone, 25% yeast extract, 25% sodium chloride, physical appearance: dust, type of packaging: plastic bottle x 250 g, Use: Analytical reagent for qual  | Importer  | Exporter  | Origin United States  | Destination Colombia  | Qty.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nustore-view - Edwards Group (https://www.edward